^warning: ignoring
--
convert_try now reroutes return/break/continue through the finally
block: the finally body is inlined before each such exit in the
try/handler code, so a return/break/continue inside finally replaces
the pending one (f() == 2 here). Previously the try's `return 1` fired
and the appended finally was unreachable (differential unsoundness
witness 5). Now correct; promoted to CORE.
